# Multi-Agent Flow System

Build a JavaScript/Node.js CLI orchestration system where AI agents run in an isolated Docker VM and interact with the host system exclusively through a custom, local MCP server server. Each mode uses a configurable AI model (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, xAI), with strict directory access controls.

Multiple agent sequences can be defined though configuration. Such as a `development` sequence or a `ux-design` sequence and a `security_review` sequence, etc.

## Terminology

- AGENT_SEQUENCE = a sequence of agents whose behaviors are defined by their mode and settings, as defined in `./agent-flow.config.mjs`
- FLOW_RUN = a single pass through the whole agent sequence
- MAX_FLOW_RUNS = the maximum number of times an agent can jump backwards the AGENT_SEQUENCE
- AGENT_TURN = a single turn of an agent within the FLOW_RUN
- MAX_TURNS = maximum turns an agent can take in a given mode
- AGENT_RUN = a run of multiple AGENT_TURN's until MAX_TURNS expires for that agent
- MCP = Model Context Protocol

## Dates

Dates are in the format `YYYY/MM/DD HH:MM:SS` and in filenames: `YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM-SS`.

## Agent Isolation

- Agents run in Docker container with no direct filesystem access
- All operations (file I/O, test execution, code analysis) go through MCP servers
- MCP servers run on host, enforce directory permissions
- Agent context cleared between FLOW_RUNS (except last 3 turns preserved for all agents from previous FLOW_RUNS on failures)

## Architecture

Create a JavaScript/Node.js CLI tool that orchestrates a multi-mode development workflow with configurable AI model assignments,  model settings, and roles-based rules.

Agents are run inside a Docker VM to secure the host system from mistakes in the LLM output. The agents only have write access to one directory.

### Access to Mounted Dirs for Agents

The following list is the access levels for the agents user group, for the directories mounted inside the VM, relative to the root of this Cursor project (not relative to the user-land ./project directory).

- ./ - project root - NOT_MOUNTED
- ./agent - agent code / orchestrator - NOT_MOUNTED
- ./project - shared with vm - WRITE_ENABLED
- ./tests - shared with vm - READ_ONLY
- ./tests/artifacts - shared with vm - READ_ONLY
- ./plans - shared with vm - READ_ONLY

The ./project directory will contain all the source code being written. The project directory can take the role of a replacement for ./src, ./lib, and sometimes ./public. The agents will see `./project` as the root, and add it's own ./src, ./dist, etc. dirs.

## Core Components

### 1. Configuration System

- Create `agent-flow.config.mjs` for model assignments per mode
  - The config defines an array of agents objects in the order they will be run
  - Each agent definition will also contain the prompt for that agent to maximize configurability
- Support for OpenAI (gpt-4o-mini, gpt-5.1-codex), Anthropic (Claude Sonnet), and Google (Gemini Pro 3), Grok Coding APIs
- Configurable to each agent object: MAX_TURNS for multi-turn loops. Start with the following MODES for these agents
  - 3 turns for USER_STORIES
  - 10 turns for CODE_GENERATION
  - 15 turns for TEST_GENERATION
  - 5 turns for REVIEW
  - 10 turns for REFACTOR
  - 3 turns for REMOVALS
  - 3 turns for REPORT
- API key management via environment variables

### 2. AI Service Layer

- Abstract API client that routes to correct provider based on mode
- Implement adapters for:
  - OpenAI API
  - Anthropic API
  - Google Gemini API
  - Grok API
- Unified interface for all providers

### 1. MCP Server Implementation

Build three custom MCP servers exposing tools to AI agents:

#### Tool Discovery

- Tools: `list_tools`
- Lists each tool by name.
- Provides the context for what each tool is used for.
- Provides small set of examples of how to use each tool.
- Provide list of options, flags, etc. for using the tools.

#### File Operations MCP Server (`mcp-file-server.js`)

- Tools: `read_file`, `write_file`, `list_directory`, `delete_file`, `move_file`, `tree`, `grep`.
- Tools run relative to the mounted `./project` directory, so the MCP essentially runs a blank `tree` command to list files and directories in `./project`.
- Enforces directory restrictions (./project writable, ./tests + ./plans read-only) - Directory restrictions are also applied at the VM level for a double layer of protection.
- Validates file paths to prevent escaping allowed directories.

#### Test Runner MCP Server (`mcp-test-server.js`)

- Tools: `run_node_tests`, `run_puppeteer_tests`, `get_test_results`
- Executes tests in controlled environment
- Returns pass/fail status and captures error artifacts
- Saves artifacts: .txt (CLI errors), .html (web snapshots), .png (Puppeteer screenshots)

#### Code Analysis MCP Server** (`mcp-analysis-server.js`)

- Tools: `lint_code`, `check_style`, `analyze_structure`
- Runs ESLint, prettier, checks DRY principles, validates style guide compliance
- Returns analysis results to agent

#### Internet Resources MCP Server**

- Tools: `wget`, `httpie`
- Fetching information from the web
- Use Wget for very simple requests
- Use httpie to make requests where needing custom headers, etc.

### 3. Mode Implementations

Agents context is cleared each time the Agent Flow begins a new run. The agent is initialized with only the tasks provided to fulfill a particular agent's role.

If the Agent Flow fails a whole run, the agent's memory of the last 3 Flow Turns is preserved between Agent Flows. Allowing fore greater contextual accumulation when hitting hard problems.

Agent output is always send to stdout and stderr, respectively.

#### WRITE_USER_STORIES Mode

- Take user input and convert to structured user stories
- MAX_TURNS = 6
- MODEL = Chat GPT 5.1 Thinking
- COMPLETE_TURNS = true (encourage agent to run until MAX_TURNS expires)
- VERIFY_BEFORE_CONTINUING = true = ask the user if they accept the output and want to move to the next step. All agents modes can use this setting.
- OUTPUT_CONTENT = Markdown file with user stories in the form of a spec with checkmark boxes
- OUTPUT_FILEPATH = `./plans/USER_STORIES_{$iteration}_{$timestamp}.md`

#### GENERATE_CODE Mode

- Generate code based on user stories
- MAX_TURNS = 9
- MODEL = Chat GPT 4o Mini (keep the busy work cheap)
- Creates files in `./project`

Code Style & Formatting:

1. Write clean, Modular JavaScript code
2. Use Latest public ECMAScript language features
3. Use ES Modules Syntax (import/export)
4. Use single quotes
5. Use tabs NOT spaces
6. Use trailing commas
7. Use arrow parens always
8. Use Object Composition NOT classes
9. NO semicolons unless ABSOLUTELY REQUIRED for syntax
10. Do not use frameworks unless EXPLICITLY ASKED

#### PLAN_TESTS Mode

- MAX_TURNS = 3
- MODEL = Claude Sonnet 4.5
- Make a plan to test according to the user stories
- Always plan your tests from the user's perspective while interacting with the system.
- Never game the system to write your tests just to match the input, without considering how the user will be inputting those values to the system.

#### GENERATE_TESTS Mode

- MAX_TURNS = 12
- MODEL = Chat GPT 4o Mini (keep the busy work cheap)
- Multi-turn loop until TESTS_PASS or MAX_TURNS
- Generate CLI snapshot tests with the Node.js built-in test runner using .txt file snapshots and artifacts
- Generate web interaction tests (Puppeteer with png snapshot for failures)
- There is EXPLICITLY ZERO unit testing ONLY user tests, via the CLI or Puppeteer.
- Write tests in `./project/tests`
- Execute tests and capture results
- Error snapshots: .txt (CLI), .png (Puppeteer)
- Creates tests in `./project/tests`
- Creates test artifacts in `./project/tests/artifacts`
- When GENERATE_TESTS passes, passing tests and test artifacts are ratcheted into `./tests`, `./test/artifacts` respectively.

#### REVIEW Mode

- MAX_TURNS = 3
- MODEL = Chat GPT 5.1 Thinking
- Multi-turn loop until TESTS_PASS or MAX_TURNS
- Validate if the code was testing real user behaviors
  - If NO:
    - Create new plan feed that back to WRITE_USER_STORIES
    - Triggers a new FLOW_RUN until MAX_FLOW_RUNS has expired.
    - User is asked if they want to re-flow, if `./agent-flow.config.mjs` has ASK_BEFORE_REFLOW set to true.
    - Only continue to reflow if the user allows it in settings or by prompt.
  - If YES:
    - Continue to CLEAN_AND_REFACTOR
- Validate if code fulfills user intent of the user stories, and the initial query.
  - If NO:
    - Create new plan feed that back to WRITE_USER_STORIES
    - Triggers a new FLOW_RUN until MAX_FLOW_RUNS has expired.
    - User is asked if they want to re-flow, if `./agent-flow.config.mjs` has ASK_BEFORE_REFLOW set to true.
    - Only continue to reflow if the user allows it in settings or by prompt.
  - If YES:
    - Continue to CLEAN_AND_REFACTOR

#### CLEAN_AND_REFACTOR Mode

- MAX_TURNS = 9
- MODEL = Claude Sonnet 4.5 Thinking
- Multi-turn loop until TESTS_PASS or MAX_TURNS
- Remove files that are no longer being used
- Analyze: cleanliness, structure, DRY principles, style guide compliance
- Create refactor plan
- Assess if plan is worth implementing
    - If YES: refactor code and update tests if necessary
    - If NO: continue

#### REPORT Mode

- MAX_TURNS = 6
- MODEL = Chat GPT 5.1 Thinking
- Report on the iteration output of the whole AGENT_FLOW against the user stories written.
- Report anything that was missed or left undone according to the user stories.
- Ask if user wants to re-run AGENT_FLOW again.
    - Give the user the option to update the original input.
    - Give the user the option to keep existing stories, enhance them, or clear them.

### 4. Test Orchestration

- Test runner that executes Node.js tests and Puppeteer tests
- Capture test results (pass/fail)
- Save error artifacts in appropriate formats
- Move passing tests to READ_ONLY test directory at end
- Move artifacts from test failures to READ_ONLY artifacts directory at end

### 5. CLI Interface

- Main entry point: `agent-flow` command
- Commands:
  - `init` - initialize config
    - creates `./agent-flow.config`
    - creates `./project` dir as well as: `./tests/artifacts`,  `plans`, and `./prompts/`
  - `run <feature-description>` - run full flow
  - `mode <MODE_NAME>` - run single mode
- Progress indicators for multi-turn loops
- Multi Agent Flow CLI Util MUST be able to be run globally to initialize and run this system in diverse projects.

## Dependencies

- `@anthropic-ai/sdk` - Claude API
- `openai` - OpenAI API
- `@google/generative-ai` - Gemini API
- `puppeteer` - Web testing with video recording
- `commander` - CLI framework
- `dotenv` - Environment variables
- `chalk` - Terminal styling
- `ora` - Progress spinners

## Flow Logic

1. User provides feature description
2. Execute modes sequentially: WRITE_USER_STORIES → GENERATE_CODE → GENERATE_TESTS → REVIEW → CLEAN_AND_REFACTOR -> REPORT → OUTPUT_TO_HOST_CLI
3. Each multi-turn mode tracks turns and test status
4. Loop back to WRITE_USER_STORIES if REVIEW determines code doesn't fulfill intent
5. Move tests to READ_ONLY directory after all modes complete successfully

## Default Model Configuration

- Configurable MAX_TURNS for multi-turn loops
- API key management via environment variables

